    "summary": "Solid '84 show with rare Wang Dang Doodle and strong Dupree",
    "blurb": "The first set shines with an enthusiastic Dupree's Diamond Blues and a quirky Brent Mydland space. The second set drops the seldom‑heard Wang Dang Doodle, rolls into Black Peter and closes tight with One More Saturday Night. Overall it’s a solid, enjoyable performance.",
    "review": "On October 27 1984 at the Berkeley Community Theater the Dead delivered a dependable mix of familiar fun and a few surprises that make this show worth a spin. Jerry, Bob and Phil keep the groove steady while Brent sprinkles in an odd, memorable “space” early on, and the rhythm section stays lively—Bill even handed out his trademark miracle tickets as Mickey kept the beat solid. Highlights include a rousing Dupree's Diamond Blues that really got the crowd moving, and the second‑set surprise of Wang Dang Doodle, a rarity that adds a special flavor to the night. The set flows into Black Peter and a joyous One More Saturday Night, wrapping up an evening that feels both balanced and lively.\n\nWhile the recordings are of fair to good quality—none boasting pristine soundboard clarity—the performance itself shines through. Phil’s playful whistle hijack after Bob’s antics adds a touch of humor, and the overall vibe is upbeat and engaging, making this Berkeley gig a solid representation of the ’84 tour.",
